: June 2026</span></strong><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA\"><div id=\"§the-state-of-games-june-2026\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset header-anchor offset-top\"></div></div></div></h2><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!X-iz!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7477ec6c-2564-4945-9b85-35102421e394_1228x646.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\" class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img can-restack\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!X-iz!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7477ec6c-2564-4945-9b85-35102421e394_1228x646.png\" width=\"1228\" height=\"646\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/7477ec6c-2564-4945-9b85-35102421e394_1228x646.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:646,&quot;width&quot;:1228,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:1392455,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://www.thegamebusiness.com/i/209268672?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7477ec6c-2564-4945-9b85-35102421e394_1228x646.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" alt=\"\" class=\"sizing-normal\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p><span>After a busy May of big AAA releases, June was much, much quieter. Nevertheless, there were a couple of notable games (including the best-selling game of the year so far). Also, a major sporting event had a significant impact across the charts.</span></p><p><span>It was also the month of Summer Game Fest, with a whole bunch of different games in the trailer and article charts.</span></p><p><span>However, we have now reached the point where Nintendo Switch 2 had released this time last year, and that comparison has immediately ended the growth we had seen in the console hardware market.</span></p><p><span>Let’s dive in.</span></p></div></div></div><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-paddingTop-16 pc-paddingBottom-16 pc-justifyContent-flex-start pc-reset\"></div></div></div>", "content_sha1": "e476c9a5bec01df844acbf306bf71e8d3b523803", "fetch_status": "ok", "body_status": "full", "fallback": "none", "saved_at": "2026-08-01T00:11:57+00:00", "extra": {"image_url": "https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!X-iz!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7477ec6c-2564-4945-9b85-35102421e394_1228x646.png", "raw_published_at": "Fri, 31 Jul 2026 15:38:45 GMT", "retrieval_error": ""}}
